course: dictionary
lesson: 4961
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be a noun or a verb, and they can mean different things. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word incense is a thing in one sentence and a feeling in another.
explain: «In China, incense sticks burned slowly, and little balls on threads dropped onto a plate with a clang.» Here incense is a thing you burn. Sticks and burned are the clues, so incense means a substance that gives off sweet-smelling smoke.
explain: «He was incensed when he saw the broken window.» Now incense is a verb, said with the stress on the end: in-SENSE. The clue is the feeling. Incensed means extremely angry, so try angry in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Incense is a substance, often made from tree gum, that gives off a sweet-smelling smoke when it is burned.
fact: In church, incense is burned in many Catholic and Orthodox services. The rising smoke is a sign of prayers going up to God.
fact: «In China and Japan, incense clocks burned slowly; balls tied on threads dropped onto a plate at set times, like an alarm.»
fact: To incense someone (verb) means to make them extremely angry. Phrases: burn incense, incense sticks, be incensed by.
fact: «Kuàizi» are chopsticks. Standing upright in rice, they look like incense at a funeral, so that is bad manners.
exercise: «In China, incense sticks burned slowly, and little balls on threads dropped onto a plate with a clang.» What are the incense sticks? | Sticks of bread for a picnic | Sticks used to play a drum | *Sticks that give off sweet-smelling smoke when burned | Sticks that stand cold and dry in a drawer
exercise: «He was incensed when he saw the broken window.» What does incensed mean? | *Extremely angry | Very sleepy | Cold and wet | Happy and calm
exercise: «Kuàizi look like incense at a funeral when they stand upright in rice.» What are kuàizi? | Bowls | Candles | *Chopsticks | Clocks
test: «Historians cannot check every part: the kingdom of Saba in Yemen was real and grew rich from incense.» What did the kingdom of Saba grow rich from? | Gold | Fish | *Incense | Wool
test: The loud band incenses the neighbours every night. What does incenses mean? | *Makes them extremely angry | Makes them very tired | Makes them very quiet | Makes them very tidy
exam: Which meaning fits incense in «Burn incense in the old temple, and the air smells sweet»? | To make someone calm | A kind of tea | *A substance that gives off sweet-smelling smoke when burned | A small silver bell
